ovider-wide evidence protocol. The final node had no failed services, package damage, or unexpected exposed service. The py_compile operations may have created a bytecode-cache artifact, but no final task-directory inventory establishes whether such residue remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-847452c2e6db4628","cmd-3f23b5d61f634851","cmd-4a00a93fd9e74be2","cmd-c75f5b2d8b314758","cmd-a9b1efbbc6184e47","cmd-5c42803bcaa04aac","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart functional state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged and observed through connection loss, the post-restart boot ID differed, and the recovered node retained the script and historical results while passing another functional run. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["There is no final inventory of /srv/legacy2/child-process-reaping, so possible bytecode-cache residue from the successful py_compile checks cannot be confirmed or excluded."]}
